  "worked_solution": "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3x & \u21d2 & {u}^{\u2032}=3 \\\\ {v}^{\u2032}={e}^{2x} & \u21d2 & v=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{\u2032}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{\u2032}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3x\\cdot {e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2x}-\\int \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2x}\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3x{e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3}{2}x{e}^{2x}\\,{|}_{0}^{2}-\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}x{e}^{2x}\\,{|}_{0}^{2}-\\frac{3}{4}{e}^{2x}\\,{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}(2\\cdot {e}^{4}-0\\cdot {e}^{0})-\\frac{3}{4}({e}^{4}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =3{e}^{4}-\\frac{3}{4}({e}^{4}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{9{e}^{4}+3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
